       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with your confirmation. I can't verify claims about patients or approvals, and the dose is 5 times the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. That limit applies no matter who confirms the order.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the labeled maximum. I can enter 5 mg instead if you want the usual starting dose.\n- **Point you to pharmacy.** If you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, the prescriber and a clinical pharmacist should review the order through your hospital's high-dose or override process. That process can do what I can't.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
